  "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\pi -(-3\\pi )=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the period, we get\n\n$$\n4\\pi =\\frac{2\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{4\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nComparing the graphs of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ and the above, we see that the above graph is a vertical translation of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ by $3$ units up. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256025/assets/2f898960995c28b1a084dd6a19afdbc275259c411350de62bcaf6061df3f2240.png)\n\nSo, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+3.\n$$\n\nFinally, $B+D=\\frac{1}{2}+3=\\frac{7}{2}.$",
